-- cmd: repl
-- stdin: type K { Aa, Bb, Cc, Dd, Ee }\ntype Other { Ee, Dd, Cc, Bb, Aa }\n1 + 1\nimport map\nlet m = #{"a": 1}\nmap.length(m)\nlet y = 1\nlet y = 1 + "a"\ny\nlet r = 1 / 0\nr\ntype A { x: B }\nA\nlet (p, q) = (1, 2)\np\n:quit\n
-- stderr-contains: error[type]: type mismatch: expected Other, got K
-- stderr-contains: error[type]: operator '+' requires Int or Float, got 'String'
-- stderr-contains: error[runtime]: division by zero
-- stderr-contains: error[type]: undefined variable 'r'
-- stderr-contains: error[type]: unknown type 'B'
-- stderr-contains: error[type]: undefined variable 'A'
-- stderr-contains: error[compile]: unsupported pattern in top-level let
-- stderr-contains: error[type]: undefined variable 'p'
-- An input with an error, static or at run time, is dropped: the session
-- is as it was before it. Audit repro G: after a type declaration the
-- checker rejects, every later input still works. An input whose
-- redefinition of `y` is rejected leaves `y` as it was, and the names
-- of an input that failed (`r`, `A`, `p`) are not bound.
